%description:
In this test the server shuts down immediately after (t = 0.0s) the starting and reboots
at t = 190s. Client acts according to its default behavior and starts sending DHCPDISCOVER
messages via UDP broadcasts.
The client gets no answer and retransmits the DHCPDISCOVER message with the backoff of
RFC 2131 section 4.1: after about 4, 8, 16, 32 and 64 seconds, and then every 64 seconds,
each delay randomized by up to one second. A retransmission keeps the transaction and does
not restart the configuration.
In this scenario, server reboots at 190s so client has to retransmit DHCPDISCOVER six times
before its first success. It probes the granted address for probeWait before it
takes it (RFC 5227), and it renews its lease without a probe.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
network = LifecycleTest
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
cmdenv-express-mode = false
sim-time-limit = 300s

**.hasStatus = true
**.scenarioManager.script = xmldoc("scenario.xml")
**.numApps = 1
**.client.app[0].typename = "DhcpClient"
#**.client.app[0].log-level = detail

**.server.app[0].typename = "DhcpServer"
**.server.app[0].numReservedAddresses = 100
**.server.app[0].maxNumClients = 100
**.server.app[0].dns = ""
**.server.app[0].leaseTime = 150s

%file: test.ned

import inet.test.moduletest.lib.*;
import inet.node.ethernet.Eth10M;
import inet.node.inet.StandardHost;
import inet.networklayer.configurator.ipv4.Ipv4NetworkConfigurator;
import inet.common.scenario.ScenarioManager;

network LifecycleTest
{
    submodules:
        scenarioManager: ScenarioManager {
            @display("p=73,59");
        }
        configurator: Ipv4NetworkConfigurator {
            parameters:
                config = xml("<config><interface hosts='server' address='192.168.1.1' netmask='255.255.255.0'/></config>");
                @display("p=73,116");
        }
        client: StandardHost {
            @display("p=205,124");
        }
        server: StandardHost {
            @display("p=553,124");
        }
    connections:
        client.ethg++ <--> Eth10M <--> server.ethg++;
}

%file: scenario.xml

<scenario>
    <at t="0.0">
        <shutdown module="server"/>
    </at>
    <at t="190.0">
        <startup module="server"/>
    </at>
</scenario>

%contains-regex: stdout
.*
LifecycleTest.server shutting down
.*
Sending DHCPDISCOVER.
.*
(DETAIL: )?No DHCP offer received within timeout. Retransmitting DHCPDISCOVER.
Sending DHCPDISCOVER.
.*
(DETAIL: )?No DHCP offer received within timeout. Retransmitting DHCPDISCOVER.
Sending DHCPDISCOVER.
.*
(DETAIL: )?No DHCP offer received within timeout. Retransmitting DHCPDISCOVER.
Sending DHCPDISCOVER.
.*
(DETAIL: )?No DHCP offer received within timeout. Retransmitting DHCPDISCOVER.
Sending DHCPDISCOVER.
.*
(DETAIL: )?No DHCP offer received within timeout. Retransmitting DHCPDISCOVER.
Sending DHCPDISCOVER.
.*
LifecycleTest.server started
.*
(DETAIL: )?No DHCP offer received within timeout. Retransmitting DHCPDISCOVER.
Sending DHCPDISCOVER.
.*
DHCPDISCOVER arrived. Handling it.
.*
Probing the granted address 192\.168\.1\.100 before taking it\.
.*
The probe of 192\.168\.1\.100 went unanswered\. The address is free\.
.*
The requested IP 192\.168\.1\.100/255\.255\.255\.0 is available. Assigning it to client.
.*
The requested IP 192\.168\.1\.100/255\.255\.255\.0 is available. Assigning it to client.
DHCPACK message arrived in RENEWING state. The renewing process was successful.
.*
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
